 Can you create a Tikz/PGF diagram of a linked list?

> Here's a TikZ diagram of a linked list:

```latex
\documentclass[tikz,border=5mm]{standalone}
\usetikzlibrary{positioning,shapes.multipart}

\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}[
  node distance=0.5cm,
  list/.style={
    rectangle split, 
    rectangle split parts=2,
    draw, 
    rectangle split horizontal,
    minimum height=0.8cm,
    minimum width=1.5cm
  },
  ->,>=stealth,
  thick
]

% Nodes
\node[list] (node1) {10 \nodepart{two}};
\node[list, right=of node1] (node2) {20 \nodepart{two}};
\node[list, right=of node2] (node3) {30 \nodepart{two}};
\node[list, right=of node3] (node4) {40 \nodepart{two}};

% Null pointer symbol
\node[right=0.3cm of node4] (null) {/};

% Arrows
\draw[->] (node1.two east) -- (node2);
\draw[->] (node2.two east) -- (node3);
\draw[->] (node3.two east) -- (node4);
\draw[->] (node4.two east) -- (null);

% Head label
\node[above=0.3cm of node1] (head) {Head};
\draw[->] (head) -- (node1);

\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}
```

This creates a linked list with:
- 4 nodes containing values 10, 20, 30, and 40
- Each node split into two parts (data and pointer)
- Arrows showing the links between nodes
- A null pointer (/) at the end
- A "Head" pointer indicating the start of the list

You can compile this with pdflatex or any LaTeX editor that supports TikZ!

